is my wife and I just celebrated our 16th anniversary

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.220
a couple weeks ago.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.380
And yeah, it's not a milestone or anything,

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.460
but we took a little trip to Vermont together.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.220
That was really fun.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.280
Everything was very green.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.340
Did that while our son was at band camp.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.980
So yeah, it was a great summer

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.680
and hopefully we have a great fall season

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.400
ahead of us to look forward to.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.020
And especially as we get toward the fall season,

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.440
I know a lot of things are gonna change

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.560
around Ann Arbor, right?

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.340
and a lot of different moving pieces.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.980
Some of you may actually be new to Ann Arbor,

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.860
new to the University of Michigan or otherwise here this morning.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.580
If you are new to town, we welcome you.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.840
So glad that you're here to check out our church family this morning

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.260
and see what God is doing here.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.660
We hope that you're blessed today

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.920
and encouraged through your time together with us.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.820
And I think for all of us, anytime we go into a fall season,

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.560
it just feels like a lot of new things,

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.240
a lot of new opportunities come our way.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.860
I want to take a moment also to just give a special shout out

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.540
to all the leaders serving in our church.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:37.300
We just had over the last couple of days like a leadership retreat that we do every year to kind of gather together and pray and focus in for the new year.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:43.220
And I'm really grateful for all the leaders serving in our church in that way that have kind of dedicated their time and energy to that.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:49.080
But also I know just across our church many people are getting ready for this fall season in all of our ministry teams.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:55.300
Some of you are here because you're getting ready to be part of Campus Missions Week this coming week, reaching out to all the new students.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:02:00.940
And I'm just so thankful for all of that, and especially for some of you who, again, might be new to Ann Arbor.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:06.060
This is an exciting time to be here, and we hope you have a great time getting settled into this new community.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:12.580
As we get started here this morning, you know, we're going to be going through kind of a meaningful time in our church as well.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.840
We want to prepare well for this new season.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:21.700
And so over the next couple of weeks, we're going to be actually kind of revisiting our church's mission and vision that God has given us.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:27.800
And so if you're a regular part of our church, this will be a good time to kind of review those and kind of get up to date on them.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.460
If you're new to our church, this is actually a really good time to find out about who we are

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:35.340
and about what God's called us to do as a church and how we live out our faith together.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.980
And then after that, on September 13th and three Sundays from now,

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:43.180
we're going to be sharing our annual theme for the year that just helps give some kind of focus and direction

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.480
to everything that we do in a given year's ministry.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.060
So those are some things for us to look forward to.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:53.260
But today, what we're going to do is we're kind of coming to the end of actually a two-year theme

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.980
that we've been focused on over the last couple of years.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:01.080
I think it's been really good for us, but it made me think about like how might we be able to reflect on this

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.660
to remember some of the things that God has done and sort of process and move forward from that together.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:10.500
I don't know if how many of you use something like Google Photos or like Apple Photos or something like that,

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:16.780
but I really like Google Photos because every once in a while, actually it's maybe more than I want it to,

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:22.280
It'll, like, send me a little notification, a little prompt saying, you know, different things.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:29.380
It'll be like, you know, look back at your cats over the years, and then it'll be like a slideshow of, like, different pictures of my cats.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.780
Or look back at how my son Nicholas has grown up over the years.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:33.640
You know, I get to see him.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.080
Like, oh, look, he used to be so cute, and now he's a teenager.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.220
You know, and so, you know, all these things, right?

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.780
And look back at photos of your wife, or look back at photos of your church over the years.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.500
Got a lot of different things like that.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.080
And it's actually really helpful for me.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.980
Some of you know that I don't really have visual memories.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:55.200
And so when I look back at that, I'm like, oh, like it helps me kind of revisit that moment

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.740
and remember that experience.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.580
And maybe even in different times, remember what God was doing in my life.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:04.920
And so we want to kind of do that together today as we reflect back on our theme over

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:08.300
the past two years, which if you've been here, you know our theme the past two years

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.440
has been deep and wide.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:13.380
We've been talking about how the deeper our walk with Christ is, the wider our witness

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:14.380
to the world will be.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.420
We've been talking about that over the past two years.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.800
I think it's been really good for our church family to go through that together.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:23.520
And for those of you who have been with us for the last year or two or so, you've been

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.820
part of that and you've seen some of that, and hopefully this will bring back good memories.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:31.380
And for those of you who are new to our church family here today, checking things out, well,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.020
hopefully this will give you a sense of what God's been doing in our church life and even

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:37.460
what it's like to be part of this church community here.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:39.800
And so we're going to go ahead and dive into this today.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.940
And I was really wrestling with where to look in Scripture to kind of try to give us some grounding in this.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.600
And I feel like the Lord led me to a passage in Isaiah 54.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:52.540
And so if you want to open up your Bibles to Isaiah 54 to follow along with us, that would be really great.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.520
We also always have all of our verses up on the screen in front of us.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:58.540
But it's great to have the Word of God open as we look into it together.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:01.440
So we're going to look at Isaiah 54, verses 1 through 3.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.660
I'll go ahead and read these verses for us.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.260
Isaiah 54, 1 to 3 says this.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:09.700
Sing, O barren one who did not bear.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.540
Break forth into singing and cry aloud,

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.040
you have not been in labor.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.100
For the children of the desolate one

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.780
will be more than the children of her who is married,

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:19.520
says the Lord.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.660
Enlarge the place of your tent

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.740
and let the curtains of your habitations be stretched out.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.100
Do not hold back.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.980
Lengthen your cords and strengthen your stakes.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:32.100
For you will spread abroad to the right and to the left

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.520
and your offspring will possess the nations

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.020
and will people the desolate cities.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:37.800
Amen.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:39.560
Can I pray for us as we've read God's word?

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.420
Lord, we invite you into this time

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.440
as we look into these holy scriptures.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.800
We thank you for your word that leads us to life,

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.420
to salvation, to freedom, to fullness.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:51.400
Thank you, God, for the gift of your word.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:53.200
And thank you, God, as well for the gift

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.720
of our church community that we can look

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.120
into your word together and then respond to it together

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.360
and live it out together.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.660
We pray you would guide us in that.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.540
Lord, even as we reflect on what you've been doing

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.800
the last couple of years, that you would solidify

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.840
those lessons, God, and you would also give us faith to look forward into new things that you

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.500
have in store for us. So bless our time together here, Lord. It's in Jesus' name that we pray.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:16.740
Amen. Amen. So as we look into this passage here together, for some of us, we may be a little

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:21.960
bit unfamiliar with what's going on in Isaiah. What's happening here is that this prophecy is

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:28.540
given through Isaiah to the people of Judah who have been exiled into the empire of Babylon.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:34.380
and the reason that they are in exile is because they had rebelled against God. They had turned

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:39.560
away from God's commands. They had fallen into idolatry, worshiping other gods. They'd been

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:44.800
unfaithful to their relationship with God, and so God actually brought judgment upon them

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:51.520
for their disobedience by bringing the Babylonian empire to come and carry them away into exile,

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:57.640
where they were for 70 years, and so during that exile, God did not give up on them. God did

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:03.780
not forget them. God did not just abandon them. In fact, God continued to speak to them through

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:10.500
prophets like Isaiah to tell them where to place their hope and how to actually turn back to God

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:18.020
even in the exile that they were in. And so here in this passage, the people are now portrayed as a

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:22.740
barren woman. So the woman here who cannot conceive and cannot have children, she's described as

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:29.900
barren. She's described as desolate. That is a kind of personification of the people of Judah who are

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:35.680
there in exile, the Hebrew people. And for us to kind of understand what's going on here, for in the

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:41.340
ancient Near Eastern times and places, for a woman to be barren and childless was something that had

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:46.940
a lot of practical and social ramifications. Socially, it was a pretty shameful thing. It was

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:52.500
like, oh, you're a woman. Part of your big role in society is actually to get married, to have

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:57.140
children, to raise the next generation. That was important. And for someone not to be able to do

00:07:57.140 --> 00:08:02.780
that, that felt very shameful and that had social ramifications for that person. And it was also

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:08.460
practically difficult because for a woman at that time, she would need to have children to help care

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:13.740
for the household, to help take care of the family, and also for that woman as she got older to have

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:17.860
someone who would take care of her. No social security, no Medicaid, no anything like that,

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:22.800
no retirement savings. It's, do you have a family that's going to care for you even in your old age?

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:29.240
And so to portray this woman as barren, as desolate, and to describe God's people that way

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:34.840
in exile really held a, like, it was a very strong visual for the people to be thinking about and to

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:39.660
be reflecting through. And this really was a reflection of the people's relationship with God,

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:42.160
that they had become distant from God.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.660
And because of that, there was this emptiness,

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:48.140
there was this fruitlessness in their relationship with God

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:50.720
who they were supposed to love and serve.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:52.840
And so this prophecy, as we look at it today,

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:55.420
it actually offers hope that God's plans

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:58.320
for the exiled Hebrews were not finished yet,

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.400
and that God actually had plans to fulfill and restore

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.000
and redeem them and bring them back out of the exile

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.240
that they were currently in.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:07.400
And so what does God speak to the people

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.700
that we can now process through and think about today?

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.620
Well, the first thing that God speaks to the people about

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:15.280
is actually to call them to worship in exile.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:18.000
And this is something, if you think about this,

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.600
I mean, it seems kind of wild.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:22.440
Like, I mean, how many of us,

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:26.460
if somebody said, if we have like the worst day of our life,

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.760
like if you fail that exam,

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:33.480
and then if the guy that you like rejects you

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:34.840
and isn't interested in you,

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:37.220
and then something bad happens in your family

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.260
and things are falling apart

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:39.940
and then you're going through a financial struggle

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:41.980
and all those things pile up on you at once

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:45.200
and someone comes to you and says,

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:46.880
hey, let's have a party, let's celebrate.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.320
Well, that would feel really weird.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.380
That would feel misplaced.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:55.260
This is not the time to celebrate, right?

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:58.500
But that's actually exactly what God speaks

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.900
to the people here, to worship in their exile.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.500
He specifically says, sing and cry aloud.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.600
And just to make sure we don't understand,

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.120
these are not songs of mourning.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:10.520
This is not cry aloud in pain or in suffering.

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:11.400
Oh, help me.

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:12.860
It's not that.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.000
This is to sing and to sing a joyful song.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:20.440
To cry aloud is actually a cry of rejoicing, celebration.

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:26.320
It's basically saying, like, this is just not a natural reaction at all for someone in exile,

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:31.820
for this image of a barren woman who can't have the children she so longs for.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:37.040
This doesn't make any sense at all, and yet this is what God is speaking to the people.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:43.760
to actually do. And further than that, he actually says, go ahead and sing and cry aloud before the

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:51.720
signs of labor have come. And so before there's even a pregnancy, before that time of labor has

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:56.260
come and the child's about to be born, I think that, you know, from what I understand, labor is

00:10:56.260 --> 00:11:02.700
painful. I don't know. I can't speak from experience. Pretty sure, yeah, okay, there we go.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:10.440
Amen. It's painful. But at least if you have a pregnancy and the baby has grown to full term

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:16.020
and the labor pains have started, at least even if it's painful, there's a sense, okay,

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:23.940
there's going to be a new life born on the other side. That joy is close by. The answer to those

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:29.500
nine months of prayer and of going through all that, it's nearby. And so maybe there's a sense

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:36.240
of anticipated joy there, right? But that's not the case here. The pregnancy hasn't happened yet,

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:42.580
and the labor pains have not come on yet. In fact, there's no sign that anything is going to go that

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:48.080
direction at all. The people of Judah, they have no sign or indication that their exile is about

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:55.820
to end. They just feel stuck. And yet, even before the signs of labor have come, God is still saying,

00:11:55.820 --> 00:12:05.360
sing, cry aloud, rejoice, and celebrate, right? Why? We find out at the end of verse 1 it's based

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:12.080
on a promise. It's based on a promise. It says the children of the desolate one will be more than the

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:21.320
children of her who is married. Wow. Somehow, somehow this desolate woman, this barren woman

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:23.120
that is the people of God

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:25.020
somehow is going to have

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.340
more children, be more

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:29.080
fruitful, be more abundant

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.240
than the one who right now is

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:32.720
married and maybe already having

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:35.340
children. Somehow this is going to come to be.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.580
And I'm just guessing, I mean, for the

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.340
Hebrew people, they're sitting

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:41.340
there, they're in exile, they

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:43.280
don't know how this is going to come to an end, they

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.380
don't see any end in sight, any hope

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:47.240
for them to be able to go back home and

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.180
return to their normal lives and live in

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:51.140
freedom again, they don't see any of that.

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:58.260
How are they supposed to have hope for a fruitful future, as this promise is indicating to them?

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:03.660
And here, I just want us to start to recognize something about the character of God.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:10.700
See, God is really consistent in his character, and he's really faithful in the way that he works

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:16.180
among his people. It doesn't mean that God always does the exact same thing, but when we look

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:21.700
throughout the pages of Scripture, we start to see that, hmm, it looks like there's a pattern here.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.300
And so for the people here in this passage, they hear this promise, the children of the desolate

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:30.580
one will be more than the children of her who is married. Well, what are they going to start to

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:35.240
think about? And when we look back through the pages of Scripture, I mean, here, let me just share

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:39.580
with you, there are actually seven births to barren women in Scripture. There's all of them.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:45.120
I'm not going to go through them one by one. But Sarah giving birth to Isaac all the way to

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:50.020
Elizabeth and John the Baptist as the one that's after this. Six of them are before this time.

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:56.200
And so it starts to look like, wow, wait a second. God is saying the children of the desolate one are

00:13:56.200 --> 00:14:00.000
going to be more than the children of her who is married? That doesn't make sense. But wait,

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:06.180
let me look on God's history. Let me look at who God is. Let me look at what God does. Let me look

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:10.960
at how God works among his people. And gosh, that promise starts to look like a pattern.

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:17.440
and so maybe when God tells me this and I'm sitting in exile and I have no hope in sight

